{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Overview
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Overview}
This project is a C/C++ course-project template: a small {\f2 utility}  library, a {\f2 calculator}  library (with unit-tested infix/postfix expression parsing), a {\f2 calculatorapp}  command-line demo, and a googletest suite, wired up with CMake + CTest. It generates two independent HTML reports for every report family (a third-party one via {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://github.com/danielpalme/ReportGenerator" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 ReportGenerator}}} and the ecosystem's native/older tool), Doxygen API documentation, and a site that links all of them. See docs/reports.md ("Which report is which?") once you have built it.\par
{\b New to this template?}  Start with the step-by-step guides in {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "docs/guide/" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 docs/guide/}}} (English and Turkish): install | use the template | from a project topic to your own project | daily workflow | troubleshooting | private repository: releases and the site (T\'C3\'BCrk\'C3\'A7e: kurulum | \'C5\'9Fablonu kullanma | konudan projeye | g\'C3\'BCnl\'C3\'BCk i\'C5\'9F ak\'C4\'B1\'C5\'9F\'C4\'B1 | sorun giderme | \'C3\'B6zel depo ve s\'C3\'BCr\'C3\'BCmler).\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAARE}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAARE}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Requirements
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Requirements}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
CMake >= 3.16 (matches the googletest submodule's own {\f2 cmake_minimum_required} ; tested with 3.31 on Windows, 4.2 on WSL Ubuntu 20.04, and current CMake on GitHub Actions' runners)\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
C++ standard: 17 by default (GoogleTest 1.15+ requires it); override with {\f2 -DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD=...}  if you need to test against an older standard\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
GoogleTest (git submodule, pinned to v1.18.0 - run {\f2 0-init-submodules.bat} /{\f2 .sh} )\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Windows} : Visual Studio 2022 Community (Desktop development with C++), {\i or}  Ninja + MinGW-w64 GCC - the build scripts auto-detect which one you have ({\f2 detect-generator.bat} ); no specific Visual Studio version is required.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Linux/WSL} : Ninja + GCC (the build script picks a GCC version with a matching {\f2 gcov}  automatically, see docs/guide/troubleshooting.en.md)\par}
\par
\par}
